docs {
  # crux-backend

  Run the whole collection, not one folder at a time:

  ```
  bru run -r --env local
  ```

  The money, time and rollup folders reuse publicIds that earlier folders set as runtime vars, and
  those vars only live for the length of one run. Folders execute alphabetically — entities → money
  → notes → rollup → time → trackers — which is the order those dependencies need.

  Everything here talks to the manifest engine: a habit, an expense and a timer session are all the
  same `POST /trackers/:publicId/entries`, differing only in the quick-add payload their
  `manifest.control` declares.
}
